      {
        "id": 19189,
        "name": "Azure",
        "username": "Azure",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-05-17T08:16:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The invader board is great when you're starting, it has more than enough information to help you while you&nbsp;learn the game.<br>\n<br>\nI don't need that anymore, and the structure of the board comes with a lot of issues and visual noise baked in, so this is my first draft at solving some of the problems.<br>\n<br>\n- Clarify fear-state. It's way too easy with large fear pools to have some fear nebulously between the pool and earned fear.<br>\n- Increase visual access to blight. For something so critical it is hard to see the grey tokens on the beige card, especially from far away.<br>\n- Improve flow. The structure of blighted island &gt; event &gt; fear &gt; invaders is all over the place on initial board.<br>\n- Most importantly, reclaim some table space.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/qu8BQRF\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/qu8BQRF</a></p>\n<p>I currently hide the back of the standing island card with a second island card, and plan to eventually make a victory card for the bottom of the fear deck.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:47.545Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 89,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 435.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19187,
        "topic_slug": "custom-invader-board",
        "display_username": "Azure",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "link_counts": [
          {
            "url": "https://imgur.com/a/qu8BQRF",
            "internal": false,
            "reflection": false,
            "title": "Custom Spirit Island Invader \"Board\" - Album on Imgur",
            "clicks": 32
          }
        ],
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>The invader board is great when you're starting, it has more than enough information to help you while you&nbsp;learn the game.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI don't need that anymore, and the structure of the board comes with a lot of issues and visual noise baked in, so this is my first draft at solving some of the problems.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Clarify fear-state. It's way too easy with large fear pools to have some fear nebulously between the pool and earned fear.<br />\r\n- Increase visual access to blight. For something so critical it is hard to see the grey tokens on the beige card, especially from far away.<br />\r\n- Improve flow. The structure of blighted island &gt; event &gt; fear &gt; invaders is all over the place on initial board.<br />\r\n- Most importantly, reclaim some table space.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/qu8BQRF\">https://imgur.com/a/qu8BQRF</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>I currently hide the back of the standing island card with a second island card, and plan to eventually make a victory card for the bottom of the fear deck.</p>",
